        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grand_view_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Grand View sits astride the Great Divide, where southward-flowing waters drain to the Mississippi River and northward-flowing ones to Lake Superior.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grand_view_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlement in Grand View was driven by Scandinavian and German immigrants attracted by logging and railroad construction jobs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/grand_view_wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Grand View experiences a humid continental climate with cold, snowy winters and an average annual snowfall of 78 inches.",
